LPlay
=====

LPlay is a modified version of CarLink (https://github.com/F-e-n-y-x/CarLink) by F-e-n-y-x, adapted for the
Leapmotor C01 (2024-2026) head unit. It is distributed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
(see LICENSE), the same licence as CarLink. LPlay is not affiliated with or endorsed by CarLink's author, by
Leapmotor, Apple or Google.

What LPlay changes is listed in docs/LPLAY.md and marked in the code with "// LPlay" comments; the history of
every change is in git (the branch "lplay" is the unmodified CarLink release plus the LPlay commits, one per change).
The original copyright and licence notices of every part are kept as they were.

Software LPlay is built from
----------------------------
- CarLink, by F-e-n-y-x. GNU AGPL v3. The app, its connection logic and its screens.
  https://github.com/F-e-n-y-x/CarLink
- DiPlay, the CarPlay engine (vendor/diplay), by shihabal3amri. GNU GPL v3. A modified version of xcertplay by
  shilapi (GNU GPL v3), which credits LIVI and Showcase for protocol research.
  https://github.com/shihabal3amri/DiPlay
- DiAuto, the Android Auto engine (vendor/diauto), by shihabal3amri. GNU AGPL v3. An independent fork of Open
  Headunit (formerly Headunit Revived, (c) 2025 Andre Rinas and contributors), which derives from "headunit",
  (c) 2011-2015 Michael A. Reid, GNU AGPL v3 (vendor/diauto/COPYRIGHT_MICHAEL_REID_GPLv3AFFERO.txt).
  https://github.com/shihabal3amri/DiAuto
- Libraries bundled by those projects (FFmpeg, libusb, SpeexDSP and others) keep their own licences, listed in the
  app's About > Open-source licenses.

